UNIT boundedFilter
KIND FUNCTIONAL
FIDELITY spec
SIG boundedFilter(array, concurrency, gate) -> Promise<array>
DESCRIPTION Takes an array of integers and a concurrency limit. Returns only the elements from the input array for which the caller-supplied gate resolves to a truthy value, in their original input order.
DESCRIPTION Each element in the input array is tested exactly once by awaiting gate.open(element). The gate is a harness-owned predicate function supplied by the caller. The unit awaits each gate invocation; the gate function itself determines whether the element passes the filter.
DESCRIPTION Gate invocations are concurrent but bounded: at most min(concurrency, array.length) gate.open calls may be pending (in flight, awaiting resolution) at any moment. An invocation enters in-flight state when gate.open(element) is called and leaves in-flight state when the promise resolves.
DESCRIPTION The output array is keyed strictly by input position: if input[i] and input[j] both pass the gate and i < j, they appear in the same relative order in the output (not sorted by completion time).
DESCRIPTION For the use case of filtering even integers, the gate would resolve to true for even numbers and false for odd numbers. The unit does not compute evenness itself; that logic lives in the gate function supplied by the caller.
DESCRIPTION If the input array is empty, the output is an empty array. The gate is not invoked.
PAR Each element's gate.open invocation runs concurrently, subject to the concurrency bound.
INVARIANT Output array order preserves input array order: if elements at positions i and j (i < j) both pass the gate filter, they appear in the output in the same order.
INVARIANT Output contains exactly those elements from the input for which gate.open(element) resolves to a value that is truthy (not false, not null, not undefined, not 0).
INVARIANT At most min(concurrency, array.length) calls to gate.open are in the in-flight state (awaiting resolution) at any instant.
INVARIANT Concurrent examinations of different elements do not interfere: each gate.open call is independent, and the order of arrival of their results does not affect the result (only the concurrency bound is enforced).
INVARIANT When array is empty, gate.open is not called, and the unit returns an empty array immediately.
